Patch summary:
The GPU decoder writes a BC3 output image (ASTC decoded on Mesa's Dozen
under WSL2, for data the CPU cannot decode, such as an image-to-image copy)
through R32G32B32A32_UINT views of one mip level and all its array layers.
Dozen turns such a view into a Direct3D 12 cast from a compressed to an
uncompressed format, which Direct3D 12 allows only in a view of one mip
level and one layer: for a cube map or array texture it removed the device,
gfxstream aborted and the Android VM went down (dEQP-GLES31 copy_image of
ASTC cube maps, RTX 4080 Laptop GPU under WSL2). An image whose output is
BC3 now gets a descriptor set per mip level and layer, with one-layer views
of the compressed mipmap and of the output image, and a dispatch per layer
from layer 0 of those views. Other output formats keep a set per mip level.
